# Announce and measure every golden run

Before a golden suite starts, say how long it will take. After it finishes, say how long it
took. The owner cannot see tool calls, so an unannounced three-minute cargo run is
indistinguishable from a hang.

Run them through the wrapper, which does both from recorded measurements:

```
.\scripts\golden.ps1 cart accessibility
```

It prints `running a 1.6 minutes golden: accessibility` before cargo starts, prints the actual
elapsed time after, and writes the measurement back to
[`docs/architecture/golden-durations.json`](../../docs/architecture/golden-durations.json) so the
next estimate is closer.

- A suite with no recorded duration is announced as unmeasured, not guessed at.
- Every `--test` suite named in the Pass block of `docs/architecture/execution.md` must have a
 key in `golden-durations.json`. `ui_modules::every_pass_suite_has_a_measured_duration` fails
 if a suite is added to the gate without one.
- Calling `cargo test` directly is fine for a single fast suite you have already timed. Say the
 number either way.
